  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{Ni}: 3 d^8 4 s^2 \\quad \\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}: 3 d^8$\nSince, $\\mathrm{Cl}$ is a weak field ligand, it doesn't cause pairing of electron.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/NqBDIyIyxDmnzpl5LYWkzWtsQzfrj9ZlmzRlmwZq6lw.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nNumber of unpaired electrons, $n=2$\n$$\n\\mu=\\sqrt{n(n+2)}=\\sqrt{2(2+2)} \\mathrm{BM}=\\sqrt{8} \\mathrm{BM}=2.82 \\mathrm{BM}\n$$\nCoordination compound\nConceptual\nIII",
